// The count of Socket.read_some() must be an integer, and an integer is an Int
// or an integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). The
// number of bytes in one result is not specified, so the probe checks the
// bound the spec binds: at least one byte and at most the Int count. A
// fractional count is a runtime error that halts the program.
// COVERS: integer-arg socket-read-some
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: true
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var c = connect("127.0.0.1", l.port());
var s = l.accept();
c.write("abcdef");
var got = s.read_some(2i);
print len(got) >= 1 and len(got) <= 2;
s.read_some(2.5);
print "unreachable";
